 ## Overview
-Naive Surface Net is a GPU-accelerated surface extraction algorithm that reconstructs a mesh by averaging intersection points on voxel edges to create smoothed feature points, then constructing quads from these points [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from Marching Cubes by generating feature points first and then quads, rather than triangles directly from cube configurations, and produces a smoother surface than standard voxel extraction by averaging edge midpoints instead of using raw integer grid coordinates [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Naive Surface Net is a GPU-accelerated surface extraction algorithm that reconstructs a mesh by averaging intersection points on voxel edges to create smoothed feature points, then constructing quads from these points [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from Marching Cubes by generating feature points first and then quads, rather than triangles directly from cube configurations, and produces a smoother surface than standard voxel extraction by averaging edge midpoints instead of using raw integer grid coordinates [S1, S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Naive Voxel Meshing](2376-naive-voxel-meshing.md) but replaces raw face placement with boundary-aware quad generation and vertex smoothing.
 
